  caseFiles:
  - title: Case Notes
    body: "\u2022 Trusted domain (case files): examplebank.example"
  - title: How This Room Works
    body: 'Six questions are waiting in this room. They arrive one at a time, in
      a different order on every attempt.


      Case questions have four answer
      choices, shuffled each attempt. Pick the safest and most accurate one.


      Messages
      and web pages are judged as SCAM or LEGITIMATE.


      Score 720 or more to
      unlock the next room.'
  firstMessageDelay: 10
  delayBetweenMessages: {x: 10, y: 20}
  minimumActivityDelay: 5
  scoring:
    basePoints: 200
    speedBonus: 20
    fastWindow: 0.35
    wrongPenalty: 40
    recoveryPoints: 50
    baseReadingSeconds: 20
    secondsPerWord: 0.5
    secondsPerDetail: 3
    minReadingSeconds: 40
    maxReadingSeconds: 110
    caseExtraSeconds: 60
    overtimeStepSeconds: 10
    overtimePenaltyPerStep: 10
    maxTimePenalty: 50
    minCorrectPoints: 150
  oneStarScore: 480
  twoStarScore: 720
  threeStarScore: 1200
  minScoreToUnlockNext: 720
  nextLevelId: level_4
  nextSceneName: Room4_DigitalForensicsLab
  lessons:
  - Correct the common belief that a padlock means a site is safe.
  - Recognize impersonation that relies on emotion and urgency, and verify through
    a known channel.
  - Report honestly and quickly after a security mistake.
  - Pick the control that matches the threat.
  - Spot fake hotspots and understand the limits of VPNs.
  - Learn that what a phone displays is not proof of who sent a message.
  learningSummary: 
  performanceHigh: Outstanding analysis! You weighed every clue against the evidence
    and made sharp decisions.
  performanceModerate: Solid investigation. Review the explanations - the subtle
    cases reward checking the case files.
  performanceLow: Keep practising. Compare each sender and request with the case
    files before you decide.
